BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm .419903 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (P500-style sytax is a modified SCPI syntax. Each command or query consists of a phrase consisting of one) Tj T* 0 Tw .948726 Tw (or more keywords, separated by colons \() Tj /F4 10 Tf (:) Tj /F1 10 Tf (\) as necessary. At the end of the command phrase, an optional) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.064215 Tw (question mark \() Tj /F4 10 Tf (?) Tj /F1 10 Tf (\) indicates that the command should be interpreted as a query. Most commands can also be) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.62131 Tw (executed as queries. Arguments follow commands and queries; the first argument is separated from the) Tj T* 0 Tw (command phrase by whitespace, and subsequent arguments by commas \() Tj /F4 10 Tf (,) Tj /F1 10 Tf (\).) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 612.0236 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 26 Tm .01389 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (For example, in the command ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (CHAN:ACT:MOD) Tj ( ) Tj (A,) Tj ( ) Tj (OFF) Tj /F1 10 Tf (, ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (CHAN:ACT:MOD) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( is the command phrase and ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (A) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.86989 Tw /F4 10 Tf (OFF) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( the arguments. This would turn off channel A output pulsing. ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (CHAN:ACT:MOD?) Tj ( ) Tj (A) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( would query the) Tj T* 0 Tw (enable state of the channel.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 558.0236 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 38 Tm 2.114897 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Just like in T560-style sytax, multiple commands may be sent in a single ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (command line) Tj /F1 10 Tf (, separated by) Tj T* 0 Tw .133432 Tw (semicolons. Unlike T560-style syntax, colons \() Tj /F4 10 Tf (:) Tj /F1 10 Tf (\) may not be used to delimit commands due to their usage in) Tj T* 0 Tw .03755 Tw (command phrases. When a full line is received, indicated by a line delimiter \() Tj /F4 10 Tf (<) Tj (cr) Tj (>) Tj /F1 10 Tf (, ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (<) Tj (lf) Tj (>) Tj /F1 10 Tf (, or ) Tj /F4 10 Tf (<) Tj (cr) Tj (>) Tj (<) Tj (lf) Tj (>) Tj /F1 10 Tf (\), the) Tj T* 0 Tw (buffered line\222s commands are executed in the order received.) Tj T* ET
Q
